-- title:
--   Reducedness of R/𝔭R for horizontal primes of the node ring
-- statement:
--   Let $L$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic zero, $A\subseteq L$ a valuation subring, and $F$ a field extension of $L$ which is a curve over $L$ (principal divisors exist, every place has residue field finite over $L$, and $\Omega_{F/L}$ is free of rank one over $F$) and essentially of finite type over $L$. Let $S$ be a set of places of $F/L$ (valuation subrings of $F$ containing $L$, proper, with principal ideals), each rational in the sense that $L$ surjects onto its residue field, and let $\mathcal N_0\subseteq F$ be a subring that is local and Noetherian. Assume: $P\in S$ holds exactly when $\mathcal N_0$ lies in the valuation subring of $P$ and every non-unit of $\mathcal N_0$ evaluates at $P$ into the maximal ideal of $A$; every $f\in F$ satisfies $fb=\sum_i c_i a_i$ for some $0\neq b\in\mathcal N_0$, $c_i\in L$, $a_i\in\mathcal N_0$. Let $C\subseteq L$ be a subring contained in $A$ whose image in $F$ lies in $\mathcal N_0$, with $C$ a discrete valuation domain and $\varpi\in C$ a non-zero element such that an element of $C$ has residue $0$ in $A$ precisely when it is a $C$-multiple of $\varpi$; every element of $A$ is algebraic over $C$; families $c_i\in L$ linearly independent over $C$ admit no non-trivial relation $\sum_i c_ia_i=0$ with $a_i\in\mathcal N_0$; for $a$ in the maximal ideal of $A$ and $0\neq b\in A$, some power of $a$ is divisible by $b$; every $g\in\mathcal N_0$ becomes a non-unit after subtracting a suitable constant from $C$. Let $W$ be a complete discrete valuation domain, $\pi\in W$ irreducible, $E\ge 1$, $\sigma\colon W\to \widehat{\mathcal N_0}$ a ring homomorphism sending $\pi$ to the image of $\varpi$, and $\iota$ a ring isomorphism from the $\mathfrak m$-adic completion of $\mathcal N_0$ onto $W[\![X_0,X_1]\!]/(X_0X_1-\pi^E)$ carrying $\sigma(o)$ to the constant $o$ for all $o\in W$. Then for every non-zero prime ideal $\mathfrak p$ of $\mathcal N_0$ not containing the image of $\varpi$, the quotient of $W[\![X_0,X_1]\!]/(X_0X_1-\pi^E)$ by the ideal generated by the image of $\mathfrak p$ under $\mathcal N_0\to\widehat{\mathcal N_0}\xrightarrow{\ \iota\ }W[\![X_0,X_1]\!]/(X_0X_1-\pi^E)$ is reduced.
--
--   This is the analytic unramifiedness statement for the horizontal primes of the node ring: the completion of the one-dimensional local domain $\mathcal N_0/\mathfrak p$, realised as a quotient of the $UV=\pi^E$ crossing model, has no nilpotents. It feeds the length computation [`AlgebraicCurve.NodeAnnulusEngine.finsum_finrank_quotient_eq_length_of_comap_eq`](thm.html#AlgebraicCurve.NodeAnnulusEngine.finsum_finrank_quotient_eq_length_of_comap_eq), where lengths of such quotients are compared with residue degrees.
